Usage example (not a file to create — just showing how a parent would wire it up):

```tsx
<CheckoutScreen
  items={cartItems}
  deliveryFee={5}
  onBackToCart={() => navigate('/cart')}
  onPay={async (address, total) => {
    await submitOrder(address, total);
    navigate('/order-confirmation');
  }}
/>
```

Notes:
- `useTelegramBackButton` wires the native Telegram BackButton to the "back to cart" action; it's a no-op outside Telegram (e.g. local dev in a plain browser).
- The in-page Pay button validates required fields (`fullName`, `phone`, `city`, `street`, `house`) before calling `onPay`, which you'd typically hook up to `Telegram.WebApp.openInvoice` or your backend's payment flow.
- Styling uses Telegram's CSS theme variables (`--tg-theme-*`) with light-mode fallbacks so it adapts to the user's Telegram theme automatically.
